Port of _patches/typescript/023-checker-effect-links.patch (tsc/internal/checker/checker.go) to tsrs: the
Checker::effect_links field (Go's `EffectLinks any`), next to compiler_options as in Go. new_checker and Checker::fork
start it empty (None); ets_typeparser fills it on first use (effectLinksOf), and the links are dropped with the
checker, as Go's GC frees them with it.

tsrs-only: Go's `any` is `Option<Box<dyn Any + Send + Sync>>` (None is Go's nil), so Checker stays Send and Sync. A
fork starts without links, as a new Go checker does.

diff --git a/crates/tsrs_checker/src/checker.rs b/crates/tsrs_checker/src/checker.rs
